    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0124" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg74"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>April 12, 1893, the Brazilian minister of foreign affairs agreed with Conger the
                    duty on American flour should cease, and duties previously collected be
                    refunded.</p>
                <p>Levering &amp; Co., of Bio de Janeiro, and others have claims for duties so
                    exacted, and which Brazil has not satisfied.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to call the attention of Brazilian Government, and report upon
                    result.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
